# shellcheck -S warning findings frozen per (file, code), over the file set
# scripts/linux/run-lint-gates.sh grades. Frozen 2026-09-15, the first run with
# `--ratchets` on.
# Format: <file> | SC<code> | <count> | <reason>   (the reason is the rest of the line)
# The four-way rule applies: a new pair, a HIGHER count, an unrecorded LOWER
# count and a row whose pair is gone all FAIL. Fix one and lower or delete its
# row in the same commit.
#
# Every row below was read before it was written. None is "shellcheck is noisy".

rust_builder/cargokit/build_pod.sh | SC1090 | 1 | VENDORED Cargokit (rust_builder/cargokit/README), not this repo's code and not this repo's to fix. Non-constant source of a sibling the tool cannot resolve statically. Upstream it at flutter-rust-bridge/cargokit or leave it; every other gate here already exempts this tree, and the shell gate deliberately does NOT, because rust_builder also holds 13 first-party files (run-lint-gates.sh:11).
rust_builder/cargokit/build_pod.sh | SC3010 | 1 | VENDORED Cargokit, `#!/bin/sh` with a bash-ism: `[[ ]]` is undefined in POSIX sh. Real, and real upstream; changing the shebang or the test in a vendored tree is exactly the local patch that makes the next Cargokit bump a merge conflict.
rust_builder/cargokit/build_pod.sh | SC3030 | 1 | VENDORED Cargokit, same shebang mismatch: array assignment in POSIX sh.
rust_builder/cargokit/build_pod.sh | SC3046 | 1 | VENDORED Cargokit, same shebang mismatch: `set -o pipefail` in POSIX sh.
rust_builder/cargokit/build_pod.sh | SC3054 | 1 | VENDORED Cargokit, same shebang mismatch: array element expansion in POSIX sh.
scripts/linux/codeql/codeql-android.sh | SC2164 | 1 | KEEP: `cd /workspace` inside run_codeql_android, which the caller reaches only after ci-container-run-android.sh has already resolved and entered the same workspace. A `|| exit` here would report the second failure of a directory whose absence already failed the driver.
scripts/linux/codeql/codeql-common.sh | SC2164 | 2 | KEEP: the pushd/popd pair in codeql_install_cli around the unzip. The directory is one this function just created with `mkdir -p`; if that failed, the mkdir did, and the pushd's message would name the symptom rather than the cause.
scripts/linux/lib/container-steps.sh | SC2034 | 1 | KEEP: CODE_QUALITY_VENV_DIR is read by the shared code_quality_ensure_cmake_format function sourced above.
scripts/linux/lib/packaging-common.sh | SC2034 | 1 | KEEP: APP_PACKAGING_ICON_FALLBACKS is an array, so it cannot be `export`ed the way the four scalars beside it are (bash does not put arrays in the environment). It is read by app-packaging.sh, sourced two lines below, in the same shell.
